00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:18.900
In Russian adjectives like вкусный, must match the gender of the noun they describe.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:22.680
For masculine nouns like хлеб, or Sir, we say вкусный.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.220
For feminine nouns we change it to вкусные.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.500
Комперту English where delish is,

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:29.540
Stays the same no matter what it describes.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:33.220
This is like adding and ending so the words fit together smoothly.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:36.000
Вкусная еда works for feminine items.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.860
The pattern keeps descriptions clear and natural.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.960
Before we move on, here is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.360
The word Chai started in Northern China as Chai.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:52.640
It travelled a silk road into Central Asia and reached Russia in the 17th century through Mongol and Turkic traders.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:57.620
It shares the same route as the English word T, which arrived by a different seer route.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:02.720
Рашен Чай, Саунзлэк Чай, yet it means the plane drink, not a spiced latte.

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:07.920
